   "evidence": "The proof uses the restricted equivalence only to get `Module.Finite R H` / `Module.Flat R H` for `finrank_hopfSpec R H.obj x` (Rank.lean:62) plus an iso over `Spec R`. Both instances are obtainable at the unrestricted level from `moduleFinite_iff_isFinite_hopfSpec` / `moduleFlat_iff_flat_hopfSpec` (HopfSpec.lean:320, 332) transported along `commHopfAlgCatOpEquivAffineGroupSchemeCat.functorComp\u03b9Iso` (Equivalence.lean:49) and the counit, with `MorphismProperty.over_iso_iff` for the transport (already used in FiniteLocallyFree.lean:91-93). `inverseComp\u03b9Iso R` is `Iso.refl _` (FiniteLocallyFree.lean:194-201), so specializing back to `coordinateHopfAlgebra R G` is immediate.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/AffineGroupScheme/CartierDuality/Rank.lean",
   "fix": "State it for `G : AffineGroupSchemeCat (CommRingCat.of R)` with `[IsFinite G.obj.X.hom] [Flat G.obj.X.hom]`, comparing against `((commHopfAlgCatOpEquivAffineGroupSchemeCat (CommRingCat.of R)).inverse.obj G).unop` (the coordinate-algebra idiom already used in LinearlyReductive.lean:63), and derive the finite-locally-free case used by `finrank_cartierDual` from it.",
   "issue": "`finrank_eq_rankAtStalk_coordinateHopfAlgebra` is stated for `G : FiniteLocallyFreeCommAffineGroupSchemeCat (CommRingCat.of R)`, whose object property bundles `LocallyOfFinitePresentation G.obj.X.hom` and `IsCommMonObj G.obj.X` (FiniteLocallyFree.lean:74-75). Neither is needed: the identity `finrank = rankAtStalk (coordinate algebra)` only needs the structure morphism finite and flat, as `finrank_hopfSpec` itself shows. A user with a finite flat affine group scheme that is not a commutative group object cannot apply this public lemma.",
   "line": "44"
  }
 ],
